== ieee_16_12_10_nexttime_always_weak_p3
# evidence: derived
# 16.12.10 p3 (nexttime always a): as long as the clock ticks, a holds at every future tick starting
# from the next one. Attempt 0 fails at 1. Attempts 1, 2 are alive, attempt 3 has no next tick:
# all weak, so none fails at the end.
property: nexttime always a
support: oracle
rejected-by: unbounded 'always' (no upper bound) is not supported yet
scope: attempt
clause: 16.12.10 16.12.11
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.12.10 p3, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2 3
a       : 1 . 1 1
outcome : F p p p
decided : 1 . . .
fail    : . 1 . .
pending: 3
final-fail: 0

== ieee_16_12_10_s_nexttime_always_p4
# evidence: derived
# 16.12.10 p4 (s_nexttime always a): the clock shall tick at least once more, and while it ticks a
# holds. Same trace: the attempt at the last tick has no next tick and fails at the end; the
# always itself is weak, so the attempts 1 and 2 do not.
property: s_nexttime always a
support: oracle
rejected-by: unbounded 'always' (no upper bound) is not supported yet
scope: attempt
clause: 16.12.10 16.12.11
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.12.10 p4, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2 3
a       : 1 . 1 1
outcome : F p p p
decided : 1 . . .
fail    : . 1 . .
pending: 3
final-fail: 1

== ieee_16_12_10_nexttime_s_eventually_satisfied_p5
# evidence: derived
# 16.12.10 p5 (nexttime s_eventually a): if the clock ticks again, a shall hold at some tick from
# the next one on. a is first true at sample 2: attempts 0 and 1 succeed there; attempt 2 has no next
# tick (weak nexttime: true at the end).
property: nexttime s_eventually a
scope: attempt
clause: 16.12.10 16.12.13
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.12.10 p5, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2
a       : . . 1
outcome : T T p
decided : 2 2 .
pass    : . . 1
pending: 1
final-fail: 0

== ieee_16_12_10_nexttime_s_eventually_unsatisfied_p5
# evidence: derived
# 16.12.10 p5: a never holds after the starting tick, so attempts 0 and 1 (a next tick exists) fail
# at the end of the simulation; attempt 2 has no next tick and is true (weak). Note a at sample 0
# does not count: the eventuality starts at the next tick.
property: nexttime s_eventually a
scope: attempt
clause: 16.12.10 16.12.13
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.12.10 p5, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2
a       : 1 . .
outcome : p p p
