d       : . . 1 . . .
outcome : F t t T t t
decided : 2 1 2 4 4 5
fail    : . . 1 . . .
pass    : . . . . 1 .
pending: 0

== ieee_16_12_20_rule3_or_fails_when_both_arms_fail
# evidence: derived
# 16.12.20 rule3: a[*2] |-> ((##[1:3] c) or (d |=> e)): after two consecutive a, either c within one to
# three cycles or, if d holds now, e one cycle later. Derived trace: the antecedent of attempt 0 ends
# at 1 where d holds; e is low at 2 (second arm fails at 2) and c is low at 2, 3, 4 (first arm fails
# at 4), so the attempt fails at 4. Attempt 1 has only one a then a low: no match, vacuous.
property: a[*2] |-> ((##[1:3] c) or (d |=> e))
scope: attempt
clause: 16.12.20 16.12.4
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.12.20 rule3, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2 3 4 5
a       : 1 1 . . . .
d       : . 1 . . . .
c       : . . . . . .
e       : . . . . . .
outcome : F t t t t t
decided : 4 2 2 3 4 5
fail    : . . . . 1 .
pending: 0

