c       : . . . 1 . .
e       : . . . . . .
outcome : T t t t t t
decided : 3 2 2 3 4 5
pass    : . . . 1 . .
pending: 0

== ieee_16_12_20_rule5_then_branch_fails
# evidence: derived
# 16.12.20 rule5: a ##1 (b || c)[->1] |-> if (b) (##1 d |-> e) else f. The antecedent is a, then the
# next occurrence of b or c. Derived trace: a at 0, b is the first at 2 (c never): the then-branch
# applies: d follows at 3 and e is low at 3, so the attempt fails at 3.
property: a ##1 (b || c)[->1] |-> if (b) (##1 d |-> e) else f
support: oracle
rejected-by: goto repetition [->] is not supported yet
scope: attempt
clause: 16.12.20 16.12.6 16.12.7
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.12.20 rule5, re-expressed
